    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "TRANS TEXAS A\npray ong",
      "A Trans-Texas Starliner flys over San Jacinto Monument\n... symbol of the Battle of San Jacinto ... . in which\nTexas won her independence from Mexico. Trans-Texas\nStarliners .... 21 passenger DC-threes .... the world's\nmost famous airliners .... bring passenger.... airmail\n... and air freight service to 38 Texas cities .... anc\n6 Mexican border points.\nSmiling hostesses in colorful\ncowgirl dress are ready to welcome you aboard Trans-Texas\nStarliners .... so named for the Lone Star flag unfurled\non each plane.\nP1496\n\"'Plastichrome\" by Colourpiclure, Basion 15, Mass., U.S.A.\nPlace\nSTAMP\nHere\nPost\nCard\nADDRESS\nTRANS-TEXAS AIRWAYS\n2015.166.1439"
    ],
